<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Trio in E minor, first movement (Samuel Coleridge-Taylor)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1893</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Freedom (Motherless Child) (Richie Havens)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1969</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Sometimes (Olly Wilson)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1976</span><span class="sg-chain-h">for tenor and tape, based on the spiritual</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Piano Sonata No. 4 (George Walker)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Motherless Child (Boney M.)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1977</span><span class="sg-chain-h">disco version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Motherless Child (Ghostface Killah)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1996</span><span class="sg-chain-h">hip-hop version</span></li></ul></section>
